IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc24-remote.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXII.01 (Remote Attendance by Certain Persons), sections 715.21 to 715.27:
-- Principles, General, Accused and Offenders, Participants, Judge or Justice, Prospective Jurors.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of ccc24-appeal-procedure.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING; a caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE).
-- A function named "may" whose "if", "with" or "who" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12).
-- Answers named "the limitation ... is met" answer JUST TRUE where the text's own "only if" condition holds and JUST FALSE where it does not; JUST TRUE there is not a grant, which the neighbouring "may" function gives.
-- The court's opinion that an appearance "would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances" is a plain input everywhere (the listed circumstances are not an exhaustive test).

§ `Part XXII.01 -- Remote Attendance by Certain Persons (sections 715.21 to 715.27)`

§§ `Sections 715.21 to 715.222 -- Principles and General`

-- src:14783 | 715.21 Except as otherwise provided in this Act, a person who appears at, participates in or presides at a proceeding shall do so in person.
@ref s 715.21 (src:14783-14783)
GIVEN `the person appears at, participates in or presides at a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.21 the person shall appear at, participate in or preside at the proceeding in person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `this Act otherwise provides`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as otherwise provided in this Act"
        IF `the person appears at, participates in or presides at a proceeding`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who appears at, participates in or presides at a proceeding shall do so in person"

-- src:14789 | 715.221 If the court denies a request respecting a person’s appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under this Part, it shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for the denial.
@ref s 715.221 (src:14789-14789)
GIVEN `the court denies a request respecting a person's appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under Part XXII.01` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.221 the court shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for the denial` MEANS
    IF `the court denies a request respecting a person's appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under Part XXII.01`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court denies a request respecting a person's appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under this Part"

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14791 | 715.222 If the court allows or requires a person’s appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under this Part, it may, at any time, cease the use of those technological means and take any measure that it considers appropriate in the circumstances to have the person appear at or participate in the proceedings.
@ref s 715.222 (src:14791-14791)
GIVEN `the court allows or requires the person's appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under Part XXII.01` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.222 the court may, at any time, cease the use of the technological means and take any measure that it considers appropriate in the circumstances to have the person appear at or participate in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the court allows or requires the person's appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under Part XXII.01`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court allows or requires a person’s appearance or participation by audioconference or videoconference under this Part, it may, at any time, cease the use of those technological means"

§§ `Sections 715.23 to 715.243 -- Accused and offenders`

DECLARE `s 715.23 circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.23(a) the location and personal circumstances of the accused or offender`
    `s 715.23(b) the costs that would be incurred if the accused or offender were to appear in person`
    `s 715.23(c) the suitability of the location from where the accused or offender will appear`
    `s 715.23(d) the accused's or offender's right to a fair and public hearing`
    `s 715.23(e) the nature and seriousness of the offence`
    `s 715.23 another circumstance`

-- "having regard to all the circumstances, including": every circumstance is to be regarded, so the answer is JUST TRUE for each, listed or not.
-- src:14796 | (a) the location and personal circumstances of the accused or offender;
-- src:14797 | (b) the costs that would be incurred if the accused or offender were to appear in person;
-- src:14798 | (c) the suitability of the location from where the accused or offender will appear;
-- src:14799 | (d) the accused’s or offender’s right to a fair and public hearing; and
-- src:14800 | (e) the nature and seriousness of the offence.
@ref s 715.23(a) to (e) (src:14796-14800)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 715.23 circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.23 the court is to have regard to the circumstance in forming its opinion` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 715.23 another circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says "all the circumstances, including": a circumstance not listed is also to be regarded
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:14795 | 715.23 Before making a determination to allow or require an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241, the court must be of the opinion that the appearance by those means would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances, including
@ref s 715.23 (src:14795-14795)
GIVEN `the court is about to make a determination to allow or require an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.23 the court must be of the opinion that the appearance by those means would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make a determination to allow or require an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before making a determination to allow or require an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241"

