-- src:14802 | 715.231 The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow an accused to appear by videoconference at the preliminary inquiry.
@ref s 715.231 (src:14802-14802)
GIVEN `the appearance is by videoconference at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.231 the court may allow an accused to appear by videoconference at the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the appearance is by videoconference at the preliminary inquiry` AND `the prosecutor consents` AND `the accused consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow an accused to appear by videoconference at the preliminary inquiry"

-- 715.232: (a) "if the accused is not in custody, with the consent of the accused and the prosecutor" and (b) "if the accused is in custody, with the consent of the accused".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14804 | 715.232 The court may allow an accused to appear by videoconference at a trial for a summary conviction offence
-- src:14805 | (a) if the accused is not in custody, with the consent of the accused and the prosecutor; and
-- src:14806 | (b) if the accused is in custody, with the consent of the accused.
@ref s 715.232 (src:14804-14806)
GIVEN `the appearance is by videoconference at a trial for a summary conviction offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.232 the court may allow an accused to appear by videoconference at a trial for a summary conviction offence` MEANS
    IF    `the appearance is by videoconference at a trial for a summary conviction offence`
      AND (   ((NOT `the accused is in custody`) AND `the accused consents` AND `the prosecutor consents`)
           OR (`the accused is in custody` AND `the accused consents`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) if the accused is not in custody, with the consent of the accused and the prosecutor; and (b) if the accused is in custody, with the consent of the accused"

-- 715.233: the grant is "with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused"; "However, an accused must not appear by videoconference during a jury trial when evidence is being presented to the jury" closes it.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- @tag grant=closed
-- src:14808 | 715.233 The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow an accused to appear by videoconference at a trial for an indictable offence. However, an accused must not appear by videoconference during a jury trial when evidence is being presented to the jury.
@ref s 715.233 (src:14808-14808)
GIVEN `the appearance is by videoconference at a trial for an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial is a jury trial and evidence is being presented to the jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.233 the court may allow an accused to appear by videoconference at a trial for an indictable offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appearance is by videoconference at a trial for an indictable offence`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "allow an accused to appear by videoconference at a trial for an indictable offence"
        IF `the trial is a jury trial and evidence is being presented to the jury`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an accused must not appear by videoconference during a jury trial when evidence is being presented to the jury"
        IF `the prosecutor consents` AND `the accused consents`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused"

