-- 715.24: "In any proceedings in respect of which this Act does not expressly authorize the court ... or limit or prohibit their appearance": a where-gate; where it fails the other sections govern, and the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling (b)).
-- @tag grant=where
-- src:14820 | 715.24 In any proceedings in respect of which this Act does not expressly authorize the court to allow an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference or limit or prohibit their appearance by those means, the court may allow the accused or offender to appear by either of those means.
@ref s 715.24 (src:14820-14820)
GIVEN `this Act expressly authorizes the court to allow the accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act limits or prohibits the appearance of the accused or offender by those means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.24 the court may allow the accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference` MEANS
    IF (NOT `this Act expressly authorizes the court to allow the accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference`) AND (NOT `this Act limits or prohibits the appearance of the accused or offender by those means`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In any proceedings in respect of which this Act does not expressly authorize the court to allow an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference or limit or prohibit their appearance by those means"

