`s 715.242 the court must be satisfied that the accused or offender will be able to understand the proceedings and that any decisions made by them during the proceedings will be voluntary` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to allow an accused or offender to appear by audioconference or videoconference` AND `the accused or offender does not have access to legal advice during the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before allowing an accused or offender who does not have access to legal advice during the proceedings to appear by audioconference or videoconference, the court must be satisfied"

-- src:14826 | 715.243 An accused or offender who appears by audioconference or videoconference must be given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel.
