§§ `Section 715.25 -- Participants`

-- src:14830 | 715.25 (1) In this section, participant means any person, other than an accused, an offender, a witness, a juror, a judge or a justice, who may participate in a proceeding.
@ref s 715.25(1) (src:14830-14830)
GIVEN `the person may participate in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an accused, an offender, a witness, a juror, a judge or a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.25(1) participant` MEANS
    IF `the person may participate in a proceeding` AND (NOT `the person is an accused, an offender, a witness, a juror, a judge or a justice`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "participant means any person, other than an accused, an offender, a witness, a juror, a judge or a justice, who may participate in a proceeding"

