§§ `Section 715.27 -- Prospective jurors`

-- src:14858 | 715.27 (1) In this section, prospective juror means a person who has been summoned as a juror and who has not yet been sworn in accordance with Part XX.
@ref s 715.27(1) (src:14858-14858)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been sworn in accordance with Part XX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.27(1) prospective juror` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned as a juror` AND (NOT `the person has been sworn in accordance with Part XX`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prospective juror means a person who has been summoned as a juror and who has not yet been sworn in accordance with Part XX"

DECLARE `s 715.27(2) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.27(2)(a) the challenges related to the in-person participation of prospective jurors`
    `s 715.27(2)(b) the nature of the participation`
    `s 715.27(2)(c) the suitability of the location from where the prospective jurors will participate`
    `s 715.27(2)(d) the privacy and security of the prospective jurors`
    `s 715.27(2)(e) the accused's right to a fair and public hearing`
    `s 715.27(2)(f) the nature and seriousness of the offence`
    `s 715.27(2) another circumstance`

-- src:14861 | (a) the challenges related to the in-person participation of prospective jurors;
-- src:14862 | (b) the nature of the participation;
-- src:14863 | (c) the suitability of the location from where the prospective jurors will participate;
-- src:14864 | (d) the privacy and security of the prospective jurors;
-- src:14865 | (e) the accused’s right to a fair and public hearing; and
-- src:14866 | (f) the nature and seriousness of the offence.
@ref s 715.27(2)(a) to (f) (src:14861-14866)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 715.27(2) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.27(2) the court is to have regard to the circumstance in forming its opinion` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 715.27(2) another circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says "all the circumstances, including": a circumstance not listed is also to be regarded
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14860 | (2) The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow or require any or all prospective jurors to participate in the jury selection process by videoconference if the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances, including
@ref s 715.27(2) (src:14860-14860)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.27(2) the court may allow or require prospective jurors to participate in the jury selection process by videoconference` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor consents` AND `the accused consents` AND `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow or require any or all prospective jurors to participate in the jury selection process by videoconference if the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate"

-- @tag fork=F715L
-- src:14868 | (3) The court may require prospective jurors to participate by videoconference only if the court has approved a location that will be provided for their participation where the technology for videoconferencing is available.
@ref s 715.27(3) (src:14868-14868)
GIVEN `the court has approved a location that will be provided for the participation of the prospective jurors where the technology for videoconferencing is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.27(3) the limitation on requiring prospective jurors to participate by videoconference is met` MEANS
    IF `the court has approved a location that will be provided for the participation of the prospective jurors where the technology for videoconferencing is available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may require prospective jurors to participate by videoconference only if the court has approved a location that will be provided for their participation where the technology for videoconferencing is available"

-- src:14870 | (4) The court shall give prospective jurors the option to participate in person if it allows for their participation by videoconference but no location approved by the court is provided for their participation by those means.
@ref s 715.27(4) (src:14870-14870)
GIVEN `the court allows for the participation of prospective jurors by videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no location approved by the court is provided for their participation by those means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.27(4) the court shall give prospective jurors the option to participate in person` MEANS
    IF `the court allows for the participation of prospective jurors by videoconference` AND `no location approved by the court is provided for their participation by those means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall give prospective jurors the option to participate in person if it allows for their participation by videoconference but no location approved by the court is provided for their participation by those means"
